    "Small held-out set (16): Brier difference not a demonstrated robust generalization advantage",
    "The model uses a short physical probe result; mass and friction are never supplied to its features",
    "Held-out shadow evaluation ALWAYS executes the second push to obtain labels even when model suggests observing",
    "Continuous scenes place three static or freejoint objects and use simulator-truth pose, sparse idealized rays, reference V5 gait, and controlled bounded pushes",
    "Only one or two physical experiments per integrated scene were completed in the three tested rooms",
    "Online updating means replay fine-tuning of outcome predictor, not learning a motor-control policy",
    "Never execute these pushes on a real robot or in an uncontrolled environment without force sensing, reliable localization and a safety stop"
  ]
